@startuml audit-readback
' UML sequence diagram only: participants, lifelines, messages, returns,
' delays and notes, and no other diagram or UML element type. The subject is
' that the audit streams outlive the container that wrote them.
' Source of record for docs/diagrams/audit-readback.svg. Do not edit the SVG:
' render it with the pinned PlantUML image (docs/adopting.md).
' &#45;&#45; is a literal "--": PlantUML reads --text-- as strikeout.
title audit: the evidence outlives the container

participant "gateway container\nclass <class>" as G
participant "state dir\n~/.local/state/agentjail/audit/<class>" as S
participant "next run of the class\nagentjail run" as R
participant "operator\nagentjail audit &#45;&#45;class <class>" as A

G -> S : <jail-id>.audit.log\none line per decision: allow (resolved, pinned),\nallow-close (bytes), deny (reason)
G -> S : <jail-id>.dns.log\none line per query: answer, nxdomain, refused, drop
note over G : written at decision time, not when the connection ends:\na tunnel that is established and then reset is still a line
... run over: the jail, started with &#45;&#45;rm, is gone; the gateway, which has no &#45;&#45;rm, was removed by the run's cleanup guard ...
note over S
  The record is this directory, not the container log. The gateway carries no
  &#45;&#45;rm on purpose: a gateway that refuses to start keeps its exit code and
  its output, which is how the refusal is reported. A gateway left behind by a
  killed run is pruned by dead pid on a later run.
end note
R -> S : prune at start: keep the newest 20 runs per class,\ndelete both files of the oldest
A -> S : read both streams, newest run first,\nmerge in time order
S --> A : key=value lines, filtered by\nclass, jail, decision, stream
note over A
  With no per-run files, the streams configured in the class config are read;
  auditing stdin reads a captured `podman logs` stream instead.
end note
@enduml
